of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Yang Hsiu-ch&#39;ing\">Yang Hsiu-ch'ing</a></div><div class=\"wst-header-forward-arrow\">\u2192</div></div></div><div class=\"wst-header-notes header&#95;notes searchaux wst-unknown-notes\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14791120\">.mw-parser-output .plainSister{display:block;font-size:93%;line-height:normal;list-style-type:none;list-style-image:none;list-style-position:outside;border:1px solid var(--border-color-interactive--hover,#AAA);float:right;clear:right;margin:0.5ex 0 0.5ex 0.5ex;padding:0;background:var(--background-color-base,#FFFFFF);color:var(--color-base,#202122)}.mw-parser-output .sisicon,.mw-parser-output .dabicon{padding-right:1ex}</style><ul class=\"plainSister\"><li class=\"sisitem\"><span class=\"sisicon\"><span typeof=\"mw:File/Frameless\"><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\"><img alt=\"Sister Projects\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/20px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/40px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1024\" data-file-height=\"1024\" /></a></span></span><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\">sister projects</a>: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yang_Hao_(Ming_dynasty)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Yang Hao (Ming dynasty)\">Wikipedia article</a>, <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q107367912\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"d:Q107367912\">Wikidata item</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"ws-noexport\" id=\"ws-data\" style=\"speak:none\"><span id=\"ws-article-id\">3678073</span><span id=\"ws-title\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period\">Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period</a>, Volume 2 \u2014 Yang Hao</span><span id=\"ws-editor\">Arthur W. Hummel</span><span id=\"ws-author\">George A. Kennedy</span></div></div>\n<p><span style=\"display:none\" id=\"dynamic&#95;layout&#95;overrider\">Layout 2</span>\n</p>\n<div class=\"prp-pages-output\" lang=\"en\">\n<p><span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"885\" data-page-number=\"885\" data-page-name=\"Page:Eminent Chinese Of The Ch\u2019ing Period - Hummel - 1943 - Vol. 2.pdf/283\" data-page-index=\"283\" data-page-quality=\"3\" title=\"Page:Eminent&#95;Chinese&#95;Of&#95;The&#95;Ch%E2%80%99ing&#95;Period&#95;-&#95;Hummel&#95;-&#95;1943&#95;-&#95;Vol.&#95;2.pdf/283\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;283\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span><b>YANG Hao</b> \u694a\u93ac (<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14767791\">.mw-parser-output .wst-tooltip{cursor:help;border-bottom:thin dotted cornflowerblue}.mw-parser-output .wst-tooltip-nodash{border-bottom:none}</style><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Courtesy name (Tz\u00fb/Zi, \u5b57)\">T.</span>&#160;\u6c5d\u4eac), d. Nov. 10, 1629, Ming general, native of Shang-ch'iu, Honan, received the degree of <i>chin-shih</i> in 1580. He was appointed magistrate of Nanchang, Kiangsi, and later intendant of the Liao-hai Circuit, which controlled Liaotung. In 1597 he was appointed to military command in Korea where the second Japanese invasion, directed by Hideyoshi (see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Nurhaci\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Nurhaci\">Nurhaci</a></span>), was threatening Seoul. Early in 1598 he attacked the Japanese with an army of forty thousand men, but owing to indecision and mismanagement, his forces were disastrously\n&#32;<span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"886\" data-page-number=\"886\" data-page-name=\"Page:Eminent Chinese Of The Ch\u2019ing Period - Hummel - 1943 - Vol. 2.pdf/284\" data-page-index=\"284\" data-page-quality=\"3\" title=\"Page:Eminent&#95;Chinese&#95;Of&#95;The&#95;Ch%E2%80%99ing&#95;Period&#95;-&#95;Hummel&#95;-&#95;1943&#95;-&#95;Vol.&#95;2.pdf/284\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;284\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span>defeated. Removed from his post, he remained in obscurity until 1610 when he was sent to Liaotung as administrator. But he resigned shortly afterwards and went into retirement.\n</p><p>When the loss of Fu-shun (see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Li_Yung-fang\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Li Yung-fang\">Li Yung-fang</a></span>) in 1618 showed the strength of the Manchu offensive, Yang was given the post of junior vice-president in the Board of War and sent to Liaotung as an expert on matters in that area. After careful planning he set in motion, April 5, 1619, four armies said to total 470,000 men, but numbering in reality perhaps less than a hundred thousand. Marching from Sh\u00ean-yang by four different routes, they were to converge on the Manchu stronghold of Hsing-ching and to reach their objective on April 15. The first army under Tu Sung \u675c\u677e (d. 1619) arrived alone in advance of the others and was completely annihilated by the Manchus on April 14 at Sarh\u00fb \u85a9\u723e\u6fdf. The second, led by Ma Lin \u99ac\u6797 (d. 1619), met with disaster at Sanggiyan Hada on the following day. On April 17 the third army, under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Liu_T%27ing\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Liu T&#39;ing\">Liu T'ing</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>], together with its Korean auxiliaries, was destroyed at Dungge. Yang was able to save his fourth division, commanded by Li Ju-po (see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Li_Ch%27%C3%AAng-liang\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Li Ch&#39;\u00eang-liang\">Li Ch'\u00eang-liang</a></span>), by ordering a hasty retreat to Sh\u00ean-yang. The loss of life on the Chinese side during the four days of fighting is given in one estimate as 45,890. At the news of this disaster, which represented the outcome of the first major encounter between Chinese and Manchu troops, the Court ordered the arrest and imprisonment of Yang Hao. His execution was carried out ten years later.\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431518\">.mw-parser-output .wst-rule{background-color:currentcolor;color:inherit;width:auto;margin:2px auto 2px auto;height:1px;overflow:hidden}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-left{margin-left:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-right{margin-right:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.__uirule{background-color:#a2a9b1;color:inherit;border:0;margin-top:0.2em;margin-bottom:0.2em}</style><hr class=\"wst-rule wst-rule-left\" style=\"color:inherit;width:40%;\" />\n<p>[M.1/259/1a; M.3/223/1a; <i>Ming-chi pei-l\u00fceh</i> (see bibl. under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Chang_Ch%27%C3%BCan\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Chang Ch&#39;\u00fcan\">Chang Ch'\u00fcan</a></span>), 1/2b, 5a; Hauer, E., <i>K'ai-kuo fang-l\u00fceh</i>, 74\u201382.]\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431519\">.mw-parser-output .wst-right{text-align:right}</style><div class=\"wst-right\" style=\"margin-right:2em;\">\n<p><span class=\"smallcaps\" style=\"font-variant:small-caps;\">George A. Kennedy</span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<p><br />\n&#32;\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>"},"links":[{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Chang Ch'\u00fcan"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Li Ch'\u00eang-liang"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Li Yung-fang"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Liu T'ing"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Nurhaci"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Yang Fang"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Yang Hsiu-ch'ing"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:Arthur W. Hummel"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:George A. Kennedy"}],"sections":[],"wikitext":{"*":"{{Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period\n | volume   = 2\n | onlysection = yang hao\n | previous = Yang Fang\n | next     = Yang Hsiu-ch'ing\n | from     = 283\n | to       = 284\n | notes    =\n | section_author = George A. Kennedy\n}}{{DEFAULTSORT:Yang Hao}}"}}}